# Yamato Desktop 1.2 — Release Notes & Strategic Roadmap
Yamato Desktop Release 1.2 introduces high-performance computing controls, low-level Windows audio session architecture, interactive desktop physics, and comprehensive hardware telemetry, establishing a modern, resource-efficient desktop workspace for Windows 10 and 11.
---
## ⚡ Performance Profiling & Hardware Optimization
- **Multi-Tier Performance Engine:** Integrated a tiered optimization subsystem offering distinct operating profiles: *Maximum Efficiency*, *Balanced*, and *Full Fidelity ("As Before")*, scaling rendering load dynamically.
- **Automated 4-Stage Stress Test:** Implemented an in-engine benchmarking pipeline (Baseline, Backdrop Blur / Glass Compositing, Particle Physics & 2D Canvas, and DOM Animation Stress) to isolate GPU and CPU bottlenecks with automated 1-click remediation.
- **Real-Time Telemetry & System Diagnostics:** Embedded low-overhead hardware telemetry exposing physical and virtual memory allocation (used/total/process working set), SSD volume utilization and available space, active logical core counts, GPU adapter identification, and network throughput.
- **Full-Screen Benchmarking Guarantee:** Stress-test routines enforce unthrottled display environments to prevent Desktop Window Manager (DWM) frame suppression from skewing performance metrics.
- **Optimized Autostart Architecture:** Configured native host initialization with elevated process scheduling (`AboveNormal`) to ensure instantaneous application availability upon Windows user logon without resource starvation.
---
## 🎵 Media Management & Native Windows Integration
- **Per-Application Audio Session Routing:** Direct integration with Windows Core Audio APIs (WASAPI), enabling discrete audio session volume control for individual media players and browsers without altering master system volume.
- **SMTC Synchronization:** Native integration with System Media Transport Controls for bi-directional track tracking, metadata parsing, playback control, and dynamic high-resolution album artwork extraction.
- **Global Input Dispatching:** Registered native Windows hotkeys across system contexts:
  - `Ctrl + Alt + E`: Fullscreen toggle & Desktop Editing workspace.
  - `Ctrl + Alt + M`: Global Media Play/Pause toggle.
  - `Ctrl + Alt + D`: Quick-hide / Desktop Focus toggle (Boss key).
  - `Ctrl + Alt + R`: Dynamic procedural theme randomizer.
  - `Ctrl + Alt + A`: AI Desktop Copilot workspace.
- **Intelligent Top-Edge HUD:** Refactored fullscreen interface anchors: the fullscreen exit prompt remains fully dormant and hidden off-screen, dynamically descending only when the cursor reaches the upper boundary of the display.
---
## 💥 Chaos Physics & Interactive Dynamics
- **Procedural Element Destruction:** Interactive real-time physics sandbox capable of fragmenting clocks, widgets, text surfaces, and multimedia containers.
- **Specialized Destruction Tooling:** Dynamic toolsets including directional saws, impact hammers, and explosive area-of-effect payloads.
- **Rigid-Body Debris & Restoration:** Physical debris trajectories, collision handling, damage accumulation counters, and 1-click state rollback.
- **Material & Texture System:** Authentic physics-reactive textures including natural hardwood finishes (Oak, Walnut, Pine, Ebony) alongside Glass, Solid, Neon, and Minimal themes.
---
## 🎨 Visual Fidelity & Desktop Interaction
- **Interpolated Cursor Trails:** Path calculation using Catmull-Rom spline curves and intermediate interpolation vectors to prevent visual tearing and fragmentation during high-velocity mouse tracking.
- **DPI Scaling Adaptability:** Sub-pixel alignment and coordinate normalization across high-DPI and mixed-scaling multi-monitor configurations.
- **Architecture Hardening & Legacy Decommissioning:** Purged obsolete clock subsystems, unlinked legacy compatibility bundles, and secured WebView IPC communication channels against unauthorized navigation.
---
## 🗺️ Product Roadmap & Forward-Looking Engineering
The upcoming development phases for Yamato Desktop will expand platform capabilities across media engines, utility pipelines, interactive modules, and developer tooling:
### 1. Custom Media & Dynamic Wallpaper Engine
- **Local Media Ingestion:** Native hardware-accelerated playback for user-defined high-resolution video formats (MP4, WebM) and static photography.
- **Live Web & External Integration:** Support for live URL wallpapers, responsive web applications, and seamless compatibility with Wallpaper Engine ecosystems.
### 2. Built-in Desktop Productivity & Media Utilities
- **Integrated File Conversion Engine:** Lightweight native utilities for instant image format conversion (PNG, JPEG, WebP, ICO).
- **Asset Optimization:** On-the-fly image compression, asset resizing, and dimensional cropping directly from the desktop shell.
- **Real-Time On-Screen Translator:** Screen-region OCR and contextual machine translation HUD for cross-language workflows.
### 3. Interactive Applications & Gaming Layer
- **Embedded Desktop Mini-Games:** Low-overhead casual games integrated directly into the wallpaper layer.
- **Skill Benchmarks:** Precision tracking mini-applications, including circular accuracy and reaction-time benchmarks.
- **Dynamic Decision Engines:** Customizable auction, giveaway, and fortune wheel widgets with configurable weighting and physics simulation.
### 4. Advanced Widget Architecture & System Controls
- **Modular Multi-Widget Container:** Unified docked container capable of hosting, stacking, and tab-organizing multiple sub-widgets within a single responsive frame.
- **Hardware Volume Mixer Widget:** Dedicated multi-channel desktop mixer displaying all active audio sessions with independent gain controls and audio peaks.
- **Centralized Notification Feed:** Aggregated Windows notification history drawer with filtering and persistence.
- **Web Link & Application Launchpad:** Visual bookmark manager with favicon caching and native browser launching.
- **Embedded Command Line Interface (CLI):** Integrated terminal drawer for PowerShell, CMD, and Yamato scripting directly on the desktop canvas.
### 5. Developer Platform & Extensibility
- **Public Widget & Plugin API:** Open-standard JavaScript/TypeScript SDK enabling third-party developers to author, distribute, and style standalone desktop widgets.
- **Theme & Logic Customization:** Granular configuration files for defining custom layout schemas, animation curves, and sensor integrations.
